+/* PORT PATCH (fix 80): the in-engine (remo) cutscene camera between its keys. A cut's camera track
+ * (sibcam) keys position, rotation (Euler angles, radians) and scale at whole frames, time = frame / 30.
+ * func_005F71D0 finds the keys either side of the cut time t (f1), puts how far t is between them in f10
+ * (s, 0..1) and their gap in f11 (s), copies both keys' vectors to its stack and then loads ONE per channel:
+ * the earlier when s < 0.5, else the later. On PS3 (30 fps) t always lands on a key; at 60 fps every other
+ * frame is half way, so the camera moved 30 times a second while the characters (Havok poses, sampled at
+ * the same t) moved 60: the picture moved in pairs and the knight crept against a still background.
+ * Now, once a call (des_cut_decide, at 0x005F7254), keys one frame apart with t strictly between them are
+ * blended by s (des_cut_blend, after the three loads); rotation the short way round, before the wrap the
+ * code does next. Kept at the nearest key, as lifted: keys further apart (holds), a step that moves the
+ * camera over 2 m, turns it over 0.5 rad or changes its scale over 0.25 (a shot change inside one track),
+ * an unset key index. A turn
+ * over 0.5 rad where the later key's other Euler angles for the same rotation are within 0.5 rad is not a
+ * turn (the track wrote the rotation the other way): it blends to those angles. The camera matrix is
+ * R = Rx(x) Rz(z) Ry(y) (row vectors, 0x00054D48), so (x+pi, y+pi, pi-z) is the same rotation.
+ * Analysis credit: JonathanDC64/DemonsSoulsRecomp (MIT), docs/40 + docs/62. DES_CUT_BLEND=0 = nearest key
+ * (the lifted behaviour); DES_CUT_LOG=1 counts what it did. See DemonsSouls/NOTES.md fix 80. */
